<div class="reveal">
  <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.28em] uppercase text-indigo-300/80 mb-5">§01 · Overview</p>
  <h1 class="font-display text-[44px] md:text-[68px] leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.025em] text-white font-light">
    A minimal,
    <span class="font-display italic font-light text-indigo-200/90 [font-feature-settings:'ss01']">crash-safe</span><br>
    event log,
    written
    <span class="font-display italic font-light text-indigo-200/90">from scratch</span>
    in Rust.
  </h1>
</div>

<p class="reveal d1 mt-8 text-[18px] leading-[1.7] text-slate-300 max-w-[58ch] font-light">
  <span class="font-display italic text-slate-200">es</span> is a Kafka-shaped event-streaming broker built entirely in Rust — one binary for the broker, one for the CLI, append-only segment files on disk. No Kafka libraries, no ZooKeeper, no broker dependency. Production-hardened: TLS, auth, Raft consensus, schema registry, tiered storage, CI pipeline.
</p>

<div class="reveal d2 mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-3 text-[12.5px]">
  <div class="px-4 py-3 rounded-lg bg-white/[0.03] ring-1 ring-white/[0.06]">
    <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-indigo-300/70 mb-1.5">Lang</p>
    <p class="text-slate-200 font-display text-[17px] tracking-tight">Rust 1.95</p>
  </div>
  <div class="px-4 py-3 rounded-lg bg-white/[0.03] ring-1 ring-white/[0.06]">
    <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-indigo-300/70 mb-1.5">Wire</p>
    <p class="text-slate-200 font-display text-[17px] tracking-tight">HTTP + binary</p>
  </div>
  <div class="px-4 py-3 rounded-lg bg-white/[0.03] ring-1 ring-white/[0.06]">
    <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-indigo-300/70 mb-1.5">Storage</p>
    <p class="text-slate-200 font-display text-[17px] tracking-tight">Segmented log</p>
  </div>
  <a href="<%= docs_storage_path() %>#throughput" class="px-4 py-3 rounded-lg bg-indigo-500/[0.06] ring-1 ring-indigo-400/20 hover:ring-indigo-400/45 transition">
    <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-indigo-300/85 mb-1.5">Throughput →</p>
    <p class="text-slate-100 font-display text-[17px] tracking-tight">111 k rec/s</p>
  </a>
  <div class="px-4 py-3 rounded-lg bg-white/[0.03] ring-1 ring-white/[0.06]">
    <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-indigo-300/70 mb-1.5">Tests</p>
    <p class="text-slate-200 font-display text-[17px] tracking-tight">71 passing</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="rule-x my-16"></div>

<div class="reveal d3">
  <h2><span class="num">§</span>What you get</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-px bg-white/[0.05] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mt-6">
    <div class="p-6 bg-slate-950/40 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-emerald-300/85">P / C</span>
      </div>
      <p class="font-display text-[20px] text-white tracking-tight mb-1.5">Producer + consumer</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">HTTP/JSON endpoints. Records carry key, value, timestamp, and offset. Binary protocol for high-throughput workloads with gzip handshake and pipelining.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-6 bg-slate-950/40 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-indigo-300/85">TOPIC</span>
      </div>
      <p class="font-display text-[20px] text-white tracking-tight mb-1.5">Topics &amp; partitions</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Per-topic partition count. FNV-1a key-hash routing. Configurable retention (time/size), compaction, segment sizing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-6 bg-slate-950/40 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-amber-300/85">GROUP</span>
      </div>
      <p class="font-display text-[20px] text-white tracking-tight mb-1.5">Consumer groups</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Explicit offset commits, stored as atomic-rename JSON. Coordinator with join/heartbeat/leave, sticky partition assignment, and timeout-based eviction.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-6 bg-slate-950/40 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-rose-300/85">SAFE</span>
      </div>
      <p class="font-display text-[20px] text-white tracking-tight mb-1.5">Crash-safe storage</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Every record is CRC32-framed. Torn writes detected and truncated on boot. Atomic file writes. Configurable fsync policy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-6 bg-slate-950/40 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-purple-300/85">RAFT</span>
      </div>
      <p class="font-display text-[20px] text-white tracking-tight mb-1.5">Raft consensus</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Leader election, log replication, InstallSnapshot RPC, membership changes. RaftPartition integrates consensus directly into the partition write path with TCP transport between brokers.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-6 bg-slate-950/40 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-teal-300/85">SEC</span>
      </div>
      <p class="font-display text-[20px] text-white tracking-tight mb-1.5">Security + ops</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">TLS, bearer-token auth, ACL grammar, per-key rate limiting. /healthz, /readyz, /metrics (Prometheus). SIGTERM graceful shutdown. CORS + body limits + panic recovery.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-6 bg-slate-950/40 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-cyan-300/85">SCHEMA</span>
      </div>
      <p class="font-display text-[20px] text-white tracking-tight mb-1.5">Schema registry</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Register JSON Schemas by subject. Backward-compatibility enforcement on upgrade. Fetch by ID or latest version per subject. Admin-level access control.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-6 bg-slate-950/40 hover:bg-white/[0.02] transition">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-orange-300/85">TIER</span>
      </div>
      <p class="font-display text-[20px] text-white tracking-tight mb-1.5">Tiered storage</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Sealed segments offloaded to cold storage on retention. Pluggable <code>TieredStore</code> trait. Local filesystem backend included; S3/GCS via the trait.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-12"><span class="num">§</span>What <em>isn't</em> here</h2>
<p>Deliberate omissions — some are performance optimizations, others need a cluster story:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Sendfile / zero-copy fetch path for large consumers (tokio::io::copy uses splice on Linux for most cases)</li>
  <li>Cross-partition transactions (idempotent producer is supported)</li>
  <li>Cooperative / incremental rebalance (current sticky rebalance is single-pass)</li>
  <li>Linearizable reads (read-index or read-leases)</li>
  <li>Full S3/GCS tiered storage backend (trait is pluggable; local backend shipped)</li>
</ul>

<div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-400/[0.06] ring-1 ring-emerald-400/20 mt-6">
  <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-emerald-300 mt-0.5">Shipped</span>
  <p class="text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-slate-200">
    CRC-framed segmented log, time/size retention + log compaction, Prometheus /metrics (14 series), TLS, bearer-token auth + ACLs + per-key rate limits, idempotent producer, binary protocol with gzip handshake + pipelining, <strong>Raft consensus</strong> (leader election, log replication, InstallSnapshot, membership changes), <strong>RaftPartition</strong> with TCP transport, consumer-group coordinator with sticky assignment, /healthz + /readyz, SIGTERM + drain shutdown, CORS + body limits + panic recovery, <strong>schema registry</strong> with backward-compatibility checks, <strong>tiered storage</strong> with cold offload, <strong>CI pipeline</strong> (fmt, clippy, test, cargo-deny).
  </p>
</div>

<h2><span class="num">§</span>Workspace at a glance</h2>
<div class="codeblock">
  <div class="codeblock-bar">
    <span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span>
    <span class="label">tree</span>
    <span class="lang">layout</span>
  </div>
<pre><span class="c-em">es/</span>
├── <span class="c-fn">Cargo.toml</span>           <span class="c-com"># workspace</span>
├── <span class="c-fn">Makefile</span>             <span class="c-com"># build · run-broker · demo · test · lint · fmt · audit · clean</span>
├── <span class="c-fn">.github/workflows/</span>   <span class="c-com"># CI: fmt, clippy, test, cargo-deny</span>
├── scripts/
│   └── <span class="c-fn">demo.sh</span>          <span class="c-com"># end-to-end smoke run</span>
├── crates/
│   ├── <span class="c-key">es-protocol</span>      <span class="c-com"># serde DTOs + binary wire format</span>
│   ├── <span class="c-key">es-broker</span>        <span class="c-com"># broker engine (30 files, ~10k lines)</span>
│   │   ├── src/
│   │   │   ├── <span class="c-fn">raft/</span>       <span class="c-com"># Raft consensus (leader election, log, snapshots, transport)</span>
│   │   │   ├── <span class="c-fn">storage/</span>    <span class="c-com"># segment log, CRC records, sparse index, recovery</span>
│   │   │   ├── <span class="c-fn">schema.rs</span>   <span class="c-com"># schema registry + compatibility checks</span>
│   │   │   ├── <span class="c-fn">tiered_storage.rs</span> <span class="c-com"># cold storage offload trait + local backend</span>
│   │   │   └── <span class="c-fn">http/</span>       <span class="c-com"># axum router + handlers (13 endpoints)</span>
│   │   └── tests/         <span class="c-com"># 71 integration tests</span>
│   └── <span class="c-key">es-cli</span>           <span class="c-com"># the `es` binary (reqwest wrapper)</span>
└── data/                  <span class="c-com"># runtime, gitignored</span>
    ├── topics/&lt;name&gt;/&lt;partition&gt;/*.{log,index}
    ├── groups/&lt;group&gt;.json
    ├── schemas.json
    └── api_keys.json</pre>
</div>

